# Original request of the change
```
## Problem
`evals/review/cases.json` on main has 183 absolute local paths of the form `<private-path>/...` in 38 existing cases (review-001 to review-039 and review-h01 to review-h13), mostly in `input.implementerReport` links and gate output. They were copied from stored run records when the cases were built (#129 and earlier). The repository is public, and AGENTS.md says never to commit usernames or the owner's machine details. The private-strings check passes because it only blocks listed strings, not local paths.

## Change
1. Replace each local work-directory prefix in `evals/review/cases.json` with a placeholder that keeps the repository-relative part readable, for example `<private-path>/src/git/repos.ts` → `<worktree>/src/git/repos.ts`. Apply the same to any other absolute home-directory path in those cases. Change nothing else in the cases: ids, kinds, labels, defects, base and head stay as they are.
2. Add a test that fails when any review or implement case contains an absolute home-directory path (`<home>/` or `<home>/`), so new cases can't reintroduce one.

## Tests
- The new test fails on main's `cases.json` and passes after the change.
- The existing eval case tests still pass.

## Budget
A mechanical data change plus a test of about 20 lines.

## Out of scope
- Rewriting git history.
- Changing case labels or stored eval results. If the eval cache keys on case input text, say in the report which cached outputs these edits invalidate.
```

